{
  "ruleId": "CG-PART-SHORT-LISTED",
  "ruleSet": "RS-CG-PART",
  "_note": "A short-term gain on an equity share whose sale bore securities transaction tax is the listed-equity short-term part (D-289). TY 2026-27: Income-tax Act, 2025 s.196(1) (p.220): \"arising from the transfer of a short-term capital asset–– (a) being an equity share in a company or a unit of an equity oriented fund or a unit of a business trust; and (b) the transaction of sale of such equity share or unit is chargeable to securities transaction tax under Chapter VII of the Finance (No. 2) Act, 2004\". TY 2025-26: Income-tax Act, 1961 s.111A(1), the same condition (thc copy p.461). Equity shares only: a fund or business-trust unit has no row until the instrument registry classifies it, so it is refused. Sources: docs/taxplanning-build/sources/2026-10-18-capital-gains-basis.md rows 1, 4–9.",
